$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$["4.5"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>The correct answer is 4.5. According to the properties of right triangles, <span class="italic">BD</span> divides triangle <span class="italic">ABC</span> into two similar triangles, <span class="italic">ABD</span> and <span class="italic">BCD</span>. The corresponding sides of <span class="italic">ABD</span> and <span class="italic">BCD</span> are proportional, so the ratio of <span class="italic">BD</span> to <span class="italic">AD</span> is the same as the ratio of <span class="italic">DC</span> to <span class="italic">BD</span>. Expressing this information as a proportion gives <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6a3fbec3/img_004_dd2b914e.png" alt="six eighths equals, the fraction D C, over 6"></span>. Solving the proportion for <span class="italic">DC</span> results in <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6a3fbec3/img_005_2044e65b.png" alt="D C equals 4 point 5"></span>. Note that 4.5 and 9/2 are examples of ways to enter a correct answer.</p>
