$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">In the figure above, segments <span class="italic">AE</span> and <span class="italic">BD</span> are parallel. If angle <span class="italic">BDC</span> measures 58&deg; and angle <span class="italic">ACE</span> measures 62&deg;, what is the measure of angle <span class="italic">CAE </span>?</p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">58&deg;</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">60&deg;</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">62&deg;</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">120&deg;</p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is correct. It&rsquo;s given that angle <span class="italic">ACE</span> measures <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6dd463ca/img_001_497b079a.png" alt="62 degrees"></span>. Since segments <span class="italic">AE</span> and <span class="italic">BD</span> are parallel, angles <span class="italic">BDC</span> and <span class="italic">CEA</span> are congruent. Therefore, angle <span class="italic">CEA</span> measures <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6dd463ca/img_002_09cc6679.png" alt="58 degrees"></span>. The sum of the measures of angles <span class="italic">ACE</span>, <span class="italic">CEA</span>, and <span class="italic">CAE</span> is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6dd463ca/img_003_429202ed.png" alt="180 degrees "></span> since the sum of the interior angles of triangle <span class="italic">ACE</span> is equal to <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6dd463ca/img_004_429202ed.png" alt="180 degrees "></span>. Let the measure of angle <span class="italic">CAE</span> be <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6dd463ca/img_005_2e99d9a6.png" alt="x degrees"></span>. Therefore, <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6dd463ca/img_006_7f28a511.png" alt="62 plus 58, plus x, equals 180"></span>, which simplifies to <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6dd463ca/img_007_0b31d170.png" alt="x equals 60"></span>. Thus, the measure of angle <span class="italic">CAE</span> is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6dd463ca/img_008_1725b68a.png" alt="60 degrees"></span>.<p>Choice A is incorrect. This is the measure of angle <span class="italic">A</span><span class="italic">EC</span>, not that of angle <span class="italic">CAE</span>. Choice C is incorrect. This is the measure of angle <span class="italic">ACE</span>, not that of <span class="italic">CAE</span>. Choice D is incorrect. This is the sum of the measures of angles <span class="italic">ACE</span> and <span class="italic">CEA</span>.</p></p>
$SATQ$, false, 9, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$Multiple Choice$SATQ$, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ${"questionId":"6dd463ca","external_id":null,"disclosed_item_id":"029403-DC","source":"disclosed","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.B.","skill_desc":"Lines, angles, and triangles","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<div class=\"stimulus_reference \">\n        <div class=\"standalone_image \">\n          <img src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6dd463ca/img_000_f2b1d686.png\" alt=\"The figure presents triangle A C E, where side A E is horizontal and vertex E is to the right of vertex A. Vertex C lies above side A E. Point B lies on side A C, point D lies on side C E, and line segment B D is drawn. A note states that the figure is not drawn to scale.\" width=\"143\" height=\"135\">\n        </div>\n      </div>\n","stem":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">In the figure above, segments <span class=\"italic\">AE</span> and <span class=\"italic\">BD</span> are parallel. If angle <span class=\"italic\">BDC</span> measures 58&deg; and angle <span class=\"italic\">ACE</span> measures 62&deg;, what is the measure of angle <span class=\"italic\">CAE </span>?</p>\n","answerOptions":[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">58&deg;</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">60&deg;</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">62&deg;</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">120&deg;</p>\n"}],"keys":null,"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is correct. It&rsquo;s given that angle <span class=\"italic\">ACE</span> measures <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6dd463ca/img_001_497b079a.png\" alt=\"62 degrees\"></span>. Since segments <span class=\"italic\">AE</span> and <span class=\"italic\">BD</span> are parallel, angles <span class=\"italic\">BDC</span> and <span class=\"italic\">CEA</span> are congruent. Therefore, angle <span class=\"italic\">CEA</span> measures <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6dd463ca/img_002_09cc6679.png\" alt=\"58 degrees\"></span>. The sum of the measures of angles <span class=\"italic\">ACE</span>, <span class=\"italic\">CEA</span>, and <span class=\"italic\">CAE</span> is <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6dd463ca/img_003_429202ed.png\" alt=\"180 degrees \"></span> since the sum of the interior angles of triangle <span class=\"italic\">ACE</span> is equal to <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6dd463ca/img_004_429202ed.png\" alt=\"180 degrees \"></span>. Let the measure of angle <span class=\"italic\">CAE</span> be <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6dd463ca/img_005_2e99d9a6.png\" alt=\"x degrees\"></span>. Therefore, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6dd463ca/img_006_7f28a511.png\" alt=\"62 plus 58, plus x, equals 180\"></span>, which simplifies to <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6dd463ca/img_007_0b31d170.png\" alt=\"x equals 60\"></span>. Thus, the measure of angle <span class=\"italic\">CAE</span> is <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6dd463ca/img_008_1725b68a.png\" alt=\"60 degrees\"></span>.<p>Choice A is incorrect. This is the measure of angle <span class=\"italic\">A</span><span class=\"italic\">EC</span>, not that of angle <span class=\"italic\">CAE</span>. Choice C is incorrect. This is the measure of angle <span class=\"italic\">ACE</span>, not that of <span class=\"italic\">CAE</span>. Choice D is incorrect. This is the sum of the measures of angles <span class=\"italic\">ACE</span> and <span class=\"italic\">CEA</span>.</p></p>\n","answer_style":"Multiple Choice","section":"Math","image_count":9,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959625,"pPcc":"SAT#S","questionId":"6dd463ca","skill_cd":"S.B.","score_band_range_cd":4,"skill_desc":"Lines, angles, and triangles","createDate":1691007959625,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Geometry and Trigonometry","ibn":"029403-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"S","uId":"b954d190-3e95-4dc3-99ff-0ad88a319ecc","difficulty":"M"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"029403-DC","section":"Math","body":"<div class=\"stimulus_reference \">\n        <div class=\"standalone_image \">\n          <img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"The figure presents triangle A C E, where side A E is horizontal and vertex E is to the right of vertex A. Vertex C lies above side A E. Point B lies on side A C, point D lies on side C E, and line segment B D is drawn. A note states that the figure is not drawn to scale.\" width=\"143\" height=\"135\">\n        </div>\n      </div>\n","prompt":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">In the figure above, segments <span class=\"italic\">AE</span> and <span class=\"italic\">BD</span> are parallel. If angle <span class=\"italic\">BDC</span> measures 58&deg; and angle <span class=\"italic\">ACE</span> measures 62&deg;, what is the measure of angle <span class=\"italic\">CAE </span>?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"Multiple Choice","choices":{"a":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">58&deg;</p>\n"},"b":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">60&deg;</p>\n"},"c":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">62&deg;</p>\n"},"d":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">120&deg;</p>\n"}},"correct_choice":"b","rationale":"<p>Choice B is correct. It&rsquo;s given that angle <span class=\"italic\">ACE</span> measures <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"62 degrees\"></span>. Since segments <span class=\"italic\">AE</span> and <span class=\"italic\">BD</span> are parallel, angles <span class=\"italic\">BDC</span> and <span class=\"italic\">CEA</span> are congruent. Therefore, angle <span class=\"italic\">CEA</span> measures <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"58 degrees\"></span>. The sum of the measures of angles <span class=\"italic\">ACE</span>, <span class=\"italic\">CEA</span>, and <span class=\"italic\">CAE</span> is <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"180 degrees \"></span> since the sum of the interior angles of triangle <span class=\"italic\">ACE</span> is equal to <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"180 degrees \"></span>. Let the measure of angle <span class=\"italic\">CAE</span> be <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x degrees\"></span>. Therefore, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"62 plus 58, plus x, equals 180\"></span>, which simplifies to <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x equals 60\"></span>. Thus, the measure of angle <span class=\"italic\">CAE</span> is <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"60 degrees\"></span>.<p>Choice A is incorrect. This is the measure of angle <span class=\"italic\">A</span><span class=\"italic\">EC</span>, not that of angle <span class=\"italic\">CAE</span>. Choice C is incorrect. This is the measure of angle <span class=\"italic\">ACE</span>, not that of <span class=\"italic\">CAE</span>. Choice D is incorrect. This is the sum of the measures of angles <span class=\"italic\">ACE</span> and <span class=\"italic\">CEA</span>.</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959625,"updateDate":1691007959625}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959625, 1691007959625),
