336.475-.613,1-.833,1.575-.22.575-.385,1.153-.495,1.733s-.165,1.115-.165,1.605c0,.68.105,1.235.315,1.665.21.43.497.745.862.945s.768.3,1.207.3Z" stroke-width="0"></path></svg><div role="region" aria-label="Long description for triangle upper P upper Q upper R" class="sr-only"><ul><li>The measure of angle upper P is 24°.</li><li>The measure of angle upper Q is 132°.</li><li>The measure of angle upper R is x°.</li><li>A note indicates the figure is not drawn to scale.</li></ul></div></figure></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">In the triangle shown, <math alttext="upper P upper Q equals upper Q upper R"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<mi>P</mi>
		<mi>Q</mi>
	</mrow>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mrow>
		<mi>Q</mi>
		<mi>R</mi>
	</mrow>
</mrow>
</math>. What is the value of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"164353ec-5ca9-46a8-bacc-4d01343fd681","content":"<p><math alttext=\"156\"><mn>156</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"89e0532f-4d07-419a-b53b-9cf1232ebc95","content":"<p><math alttext=\"66\"><mn>66</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"e7b601d7-7115-4814-ba72-7f260e0c23b2","content":"<p><math alttext=\"48\"><mn>48</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"57adc815-4355-4b5e-8fa1-1e6602f1482a","content":"<p><math alttext=\"24\"><mn>24</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["57adc815-4355-4b5e-8fa1-1e6602f1482a"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is correct. The sum of the angle measures of a triangle is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="180 degree"><mn>180</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. It&rsquo;s given that the measure of angle <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper Q"><mi>Q</mi></math> is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="132 degree"><mn>132</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>,&nbsp;the measure of angle <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper P"><mi>P</mi></math> is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="24 degree"><mn>24</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>, and the measure of angle <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper R"><mi>R</mi></math> is&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x degree"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. It follows that&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x plus 132 plus 24 equals 180"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>132</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>180</mn></math>, or&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x plus 152 equals 180"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>152</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>180</mn></math>. Subtracting&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="152"><mn>152</mn></math> from both sides of this equation yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x equals 24"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>24</mn></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Alternate approach: It&rsquo;s given that in the triangle shown, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper P upper Q equals upper Q upper R"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi></math>. Thus, triangle <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper P upper Q upper R"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi></math> is an isosceles triangle. Since base angles of an isosceles triangle are congruent, the measure of angle <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper P"><mi>P</mi></math> is equal to the measure of angle <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper R"><mi>R</mi></math>. Therefore, the measure of angle <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper R"><mi>R</mi></math> is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="24 degree"><mn>24</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>, and the value of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x"><mi>x</mi></math> is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="24"><mn>24</mn></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. This is the sum of the measures, in degrees, of angles <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper Q"><mi>Q</mi></math> and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper P"><mi>P</mi></math>, not the measure, in degrees, of angle <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper R"><mi>R</mi></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect. This is the sum of the measures, in degrees, of angles <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper P"><mi>P</mi></math> and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper R"><mi>R</mi></math>, not the measure, in degrees, of angle <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper R"><mi>R</mi></math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"7268586c","external_id":"96a4ec26-6ad9-4b3b-9ae1-693feee5691e","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"7264c04d-70a6-4525-9e24-68bc4918430f","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.B.","skill_desc":"Lines, angles, and triangles","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":2,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><figure class='image'><svg id=\"uuid-75cee175-612b-46a5-bddf-063a23356f3d\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"301.059\" height=\"148.526\" viewBox=\"0 0 301.059 148.526\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Triangle upper P upper Q upper R. Refer to long description.\"><path d=\"m38.271,144.925v-.63h.195c.23,0,.437-.024.623-.075.185-.05.332-.152.442-.308.11-.154.165-.387.165-.697v-7.35c0-.3-.058-.522-.173-.668-.115-.145-.265-.239-.45-.285-.185-.045-.388-.067-.607-.067h-.195v-.63h2.745l5.37,8.295v-6.645c0-.3-.058-.522-.172-.668-.115-.145-.265-.239-.45-.285-.185-.045-.388-.067-.607-.067h-.195v-.63h3.765v.63h-.195c-.22,0-.425.025-.615.075s-.34.15-.45.3c-.11.15-.165.386-.165.705v9h-1.065l-5.625-8.64v6.93c0,.311.055.543.165.697.11.155.26.258.45.308.19.051.395.075.615.075h.195v.63h-3.765Z\" stroke-width=\"0\"></path><path d=\"m53.451,145.076c-1.08,0-1.93-.345-2.55-1.035s-.93-1.74-.93-3.15c0-1.399.297-2.442.892-3.127.595-.685,1.473-1.027,2.633-1.027,1.08,0,1.93.343,2.55,1.027s.93,1.728.93,3.127c0,1.41-.298,2.46-.893,3.15-.595.69-1.473,1.035-2