\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/740bf79f/img_010_5476d32a.png\" alt=\"angle N P Q\"></span>, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/740bf79f/img_011_b3fe0580.png\" alt=\"triangle M N P\"></span> is similar to <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/740bf79f/img_012_b6afcef3.png\" alt=\"triangle N Q P\"></span>. The ratio of corresponding sides of similar triangles is constant, so <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/740bf79f/img_013_482b0810.png\" alt=\"the length of line segment N Q over the length of line segment M N equals the length of line segment N P over the length of line segment M P\"></span>. Since <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/740bf79f/img_014_c03aea49.png\" alt=\"M P equals 5\"></span> and it&rsquo;s given that <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/740bf79f/img_015_2bce2b8e.png\" alt=\"the length of line segment M N equals 3\"></span> and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/740bf79f/img_016_858b0dc0.png\" alt=\"the length of line segment N P equals 4\"></span>, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/740bf79f/img_017_f80c479e.png\" alt=\"the length of line segment N Q, over 3, equals 4 over 5\"></span>. Solving for <span class=\"italic\">NQ</span> results in <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/740bf79f/img_018_e430f791.png\" alt=\"the length of line segment N Q equals 12 over 5\"></span>, or 2.4.<p>Choices A, B, and D are incorrect and may result from setting up incorrect ratios.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n","answer_style":"Multiple Choice","section":"Math","image_count":19,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959617,"pPcc":"SAT#S","questionId":"740bf79f","skill_cd":"S.B.","score_band_range_cd":7,"skill_desc":"Lines, angles, and triangles","createDate":1691007959617,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Geometry and Trigonometry","ibn":"022197-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"S","uId":"51e437c3-a650-412c-83e1-e5b6ff0bc77b","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"022197-DC","section":"Math","body":"<div class=\"stimulus_reference \">\n\t<div class=\"standalone_image \"><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"The figure presents right triangle M N P. Side M P is horizontal, with vertex M to the left of vertex P. Vertex N lies above side M P, and angle N is a right angle. Point Q lies on horizontal side M P directly below vertex N. Vertical line segment N Q is drawn, forming right triangles M N Q and Q N P. Side M N is labeled 3 and side N P is labeled 4.\" width=\"135\" height=\"79\"></div>\n</div>\n","prompt":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">In the figure above, what is the length of <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"line segment NQ\"></span></span> ?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"Multiple Choice","choices":{"a":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">2.2</p>\n"},"b":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">2.3</p>\n"},"c":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">2.4</p>\n"},"d":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">2.5</p>\n"}},"correct_choice":"c","rationale":"<p>Choice C is correct. First, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"line segment M P\"></span> is the hypotenuse of right <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"triangle M N P\"></span>, whose legs have lengths 3 and 4. Therefore, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"open parenthesis, the length of line segment M P, close parenthesis, squared, equals, 3 squared plus 4 squared\"></span>, so <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"open parenthesis, the length of line segment M P, close parenthesis, squared, equals 25\"></span> and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the length of line segment M P equals 5\"></span>. Second, because <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"angle M N P\"></span> corresponds to <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"angle N Q P\"></span> and because <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"angle M P N\"></span> corresponds to <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"angle N P Q\"></span>, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"triangle M N P\"></span> is similar to <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"triangle N Q P\"></span>. The ratio of corresponding sides of similar triangles is constant, so <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the length of line segment N Q over the length of line segment M N equals the length of line segment N P over the length of line segment M P\"></span>. Since <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"M P equals 5\"></span> and it&rsquo;s given that <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the length of line segment M N equals 3\"></span> and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the length of line segment N P equals 4\"></span>, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the length of line segment N Q, over 3, equals 4 over 5\"></span>. Solving for <span class=\"italic\">NQ</span> results in <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the length of line segment N Q equals 12 over 5\"></span>, or 2.4.<p>Choices A, B, and D are incorrect and may result from setting up incorrect ratios.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959617,"updateDate":1691007959617}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959617, 1691007959617),
