</math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"76670c80","external_id":"1e523d74-12a9-4f3a-8279-13ec77276c13","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"119e4b6f-ccf8-4886-a606-4f57d49e0340","uId":"cad77a43-0fdd-4c67-8802-3394ebde3285","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.A.","skill_desc":"Area and volume","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":2,"type":"spr","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Each side of a square has a length of <math alttext=\"45\"><mn>45</mn>\n</math>. What is the perimeter of this square?</p>","answerOptions":[],"keys":["180"],"correct_answer":["180"],"rationale":"<p>The correct answer is <math alttext=\"180\"><mn>180</mn>\n</math>. The perimeter of a polygon is equal to the sum of the lengths of the sides of the polygon. It&rsquo;s given that each side of the square has a length of <math alttext=\"45\"><mn>45</mn>\n</math>. Since a square is a polygon with <math alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn>\n</math> sides, the perimeter of this square is <math alttext=\"45 plus 45 plus 45 plus 45\"><mn>45</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>45</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>45</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>45</mn></math>, or <math alttext=\"180\"><mn>180</mn>\n</math>.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":"manifold","position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959836,"pPcc":"SAT#S","questionId":"76670c80","skill_cd":"S.A.","score_band_range_cd":2,"skill_desc":"Area and volume","createDate":1691007959836,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Geometry and Trigonometry","ibn":null,"external_id":"1e523d74-12a9-4f3a-8279-13ec77276c13","primary_class_cd":"S","uId":"cad77a43-0fdd-4c67-8802-3394ebde3285","difficulty":"E"},"raw_detail":{"keys":["180"],"rationale":"<p>The correct answer is <math alttext=\"180\"><mn>180</mn>\n</math>. The perimeter of a polygon is equal to the sum of the lengths of the sides of the polygon. It&rsquo;s given that each side of the square has a length of <math alttext=\"45\"><mn>45</mn>\n</math>. Since a square is a polygon with <math alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn>\n</math> sides, the perimeter of this square is <math alttext=\"45 plus 45 plus 45 plus 45\"><mn>45</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>45</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>45</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>45</mn></math>, or <math alttext=\"180\"><mn>180</mn>\n</math>.</p>","origin":"manifold","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Each side of a square has a length of <math alttext=\"45\"><mn>45</mn>\n</math>. What is the perimeter of this square?</p>","externalid":"1e523d74-12a9-4f3a-8279-13ec77276c13","templateid":"b286be59-28b6-4c05-bc1f-1523ce2e4cda","vaultid":"119e4b6f-ccf8-4886-a606-4f57d49e0340","type":"spr","answerOptions":[],"correct_answer":["180"]},"createDate":1691007959836,"updateDate":1691007959836}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959836, 1691007959836),
