1c0,.1.1.2.31.281a2.447,2.447,0,0,0,.62.165l.329.039c.026,0,.039.051.039.155a.506.506,0,0,1-.116.368q-1.8-.1-1.977-.1-.059,0-2.384.1a.231.231,0,0,1-.038-.155c0-.245.045-.368.135-.368a2.844,2.844,0,0,0,.688-.136q.475-.135.553-.291a9.972,9.972,0,0,0,.5-1.86l1.59-7.984a5.183,5.183,0,0,0,.1-1.008q0-.233-.378-.359a2.112,2.112,0,0,0-.65-.126c-.025,0-.038-.045-.038-.135a.454.454,0,0,1,.135-.388q.834.058,2.016.058.543,0,1.279-.029T134.239,126.979Z" fill="#231f20"></path></g></svg><div role="region" aria-label="Long description for circle" class="sr-only"><ul>
<li>Clockwise from top left, the following points are on the circle:<br>
<ul>
<li>upper M</li>
<li>upper N</li>
<li>upper P</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul></div></figure></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Points <math alttext="upper M"><mi>M</mi></math>, <math alttext="upper N"><mi>N</mi></math>, and&nbsp;<math alttext="upper P"><mi>P</mi></math> lie on the circle shown. On this circle, minor arc&nbsp;<math alttext="upper M upper N"><mi>M</mi><mi>N</mi></math> has a length of <math alttext="39"><mn>39</mn>
</math> centimeters and major arc <math alttext="upper M upper P upper N"><mi>M</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>N</mi></math> has a length of <math alttext="195"><mn>195</mn>
</math> centimeters. What is the circumference, in centimeters, of the circle shown?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"91e86a83-71be-45d8-912f-5d45689efdbc","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"39\"><mn>39</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"4704939f-9a68-4740-aa50-a7a608c6ff59","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"156\"><mn>156</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"6c9c187a-a282-4a17-b8b8-827ae05228f5","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"195\"><mn>195</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"d97413ba-ba4e-4425-ab2e-007467d598cd","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"234\"><mn>234</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["d97413ba-ba4e-4425-ab2e-007467d598cd"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is correct. Since the endpoints of minor arc <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper M upper N"><mi>M</mi><mi>N</mi></math> and major arc <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper M upper P upper N"><mi>M</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>N</mi></math> are the same, and the arcs together form a full circle, the sum of the lengths of these two arcs is equal to the circumference of the circle. It's given that the length of minor arc <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper M upper N"><mi>M</mi><mi>N</mi></math> is&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="39"><mn>39</mn></math> centimeters and the length of major arc <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper M upper P upper N"><mi>M</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>N</mi></math> is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="195"><mn>195</mn></math> centimeters. Therefore, the circumference of the circle, in centimeters, is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="39 plus 195"><mn>39</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>195</mn></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="234"><mn>234</mn></math>.</p>
<p>Choice A is incorrect. This is the length, in centimeters, of minor arc&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper M upper N"><mi>M</mi><mi>N</mi></math>, not the circumference, in centimeters, of the circle.</p>
<p>Choice B is incorrect. This is the difference of the lengths of major arc <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper M upper P upper N"><mi>M</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>N</mi></math> and minor arc&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper M upper N"><mi>M</mi><mi>N</mi></math>, in centimeters.</p>
<p>Choice C is incorrect. This is the length, in centimeters, of major arc&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="upper M upper P upper N"><mi>M</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>N</mi></math>, not the circumference, in centimeters, of the circle.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"800e71b8","external_id":"b577cfe0-fe0f-4d25-89d2-bdd6eeb5337d","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"6d74e641-2ba8-47d0-b4a3-5884c627bde6","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.D.","skill_desc":"Circles","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><figure class='image'><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"141.16\" height=\"148.749\" viewBox=\"0 0 141.16 148.749\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A circle. Refer to long description.\"><g id=\"fca60ba2-a4e1-488f-a7e2-dbe04f61eb6a\" data-name=\"Layer 1\"><circle cx=\"70.58\" cy=\"78.169\" r=\"69.635\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#231f20\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-width=\"1.89\"></circle><path d=\"M74.36,78.169a3.78,3.78,0,1,1-3.78-3.78,3.781,3.781,0,0,1,3.78,3.78\"></path><path d=\"M30.078,24.619a3.78,3.78,0,1,1-3.78-3.78,3.781,3.781,0,0,1,3.78,3.78\"></path><path d=\"M106.971,17.059a3.78,3.78,0,1,1-3.78-3.78,3.781,3.781,0,0,1,3.78,3.78\"></path><path d=\"M127.959,122.443a3.78,3.78,0,1,1-3.78-3.78,3.781,3.781,0,0,1,3.78,3.78\"></path><path d=\"M17.608,9.591,18.83,6.975a15.188,15.188,0,0,0,1.53.058q.679,0,1.686-.078a.679.679,0,0,1,0,.33c-.025.155-.058.232-.1.232a1.22,1.22,0,0,0-.533.136A1.066,1.066,0,0,0,21,7.982a1.622,1.622,0,0,0-.262.562,9.726,9.726,0,0,0-.184,1.163l-.756,7.4a14.628,14.628,0,0,0-.116,1.531.652.652,0,0,0,.078.33.388.388,0,0,0,.222.184,1.636,1.636,0,0,0,.272.068,3.024,3.024,0,0,0,.31.029c.123.006.2.009.242.009s.039.059.039.175a.477.477,0,0,1-.116.349q-1.8-.1-2.113-.1-.057,0-2.