$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p><img src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/81b664bc/img_000_d066026b.png" alt="The figure presents quadrilateral A, C D F, where side A, F and side C D are horizontal, and side C D lies above side A, F. Side C D is longer than side A, F. Point B lies on left side A, C, and point E lies on right side D F. Line segment B E, which is horizontal, divides quadrilateral A, C D F into two quadrilaterals, A, B E F and B C D E." width="107" height="82">
          <p class="stem_paragraph ">In the figure above, <span class="math_expression "><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/81b664bc/img_001_b4fa4e1a.png" alt="side A, F "></span></span>, <span class="math_expression "><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/81b664bc/img_002_8b12b353.png" alt="line segment B E "></span></span>, and <span class="math_expression "><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/81b664bc/img_003_a95e1fc3.png" alt="side C D "></span></span> are parallel. Points <span class="italic">B</span> and <span class="italic">E</span> lie on <span class="math_expression "><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/81b664bc/img_004_80840f01.png" alt="side A, C  "></span></span> and <span class="math_expression "><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/81b664bc/img_005_9f84cd43.png" alt="side F D "></span></span>, respectively. If <span class="math_expression "><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/81b664bc/img_006_2e9a08ce.png" alt="the length of line segment A, B equals 9, the length of line segment B C equals 18 point 5"></span></span>, and <span class="math_expression "><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/81b664bc/img_007_2b750cc7.png" alt="the length of line segment F E equals 8 point 5"></span></span>, what is the length of <span class="math_expression "><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/81b664bc/img_008_d1467cb0.png" alt="line segment E D "></span></span>, to the nearest tenth?</p></p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">16.8</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">17.5</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">18.4</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">19.6</p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is correct. Since <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/81b664bc/img_009_884ebce8.png" alt="line segment A F"></span>, <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/81b664bc/img_010_6710a4ef.png" alt="line segment B E"></span>, and <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/81b664bc/img_011_b1e93367.png" alt="line segment C D "></span> are parallel, quadrilaterals <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/81b664bc/img_012_cd90b0f0.png" alt="A F E B "></span> and <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/81b664bc/img_013_0b4a4b68.png" alt="B E D C "></span> are similar. Let <span class="italic">x</span> represent the length of <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/81b664bc/img_014_d1467cb0.png" alt="line segment E D"></span>. With similar figures, the ratios of the lengths of corresponding sides are equal. It follows that <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/81b664bc/img_015_a646b304.png" alt="9 over 18 point 5, equals 8 point 5 over x"></span>. Multiplying both sides of this equation by 18.5 and by <span class="italic">x</span> yields <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/81b664bc/img_016_2f07dc94.png" alt="9 x equals, 18 point 5, times 8 point 5"></span>, or <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/81b664bc/img_017_b57621f4.png" alt="9 x equals 157 point 2 5"></span>. Dividing both sides of this equation by 9 yields <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/81b664bc/img_018_574e4ce5.png" alt="x equals 17 point 4 7"></span>, which to the nearest tenth is 17.5.<p>Choices A, C, and D are incorrect and may result from errors made when setting up the proportion.</p></p>
$SATQ$, false, 19, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$Multiple Choice$SATQ$, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ${"questionId":"81b664bc","external_id":null,"disclosed_item_id":"08390-DC","source":"disclosed","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.B.","skill_desc":"Lines, angles, and triangles","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<div xmlns=\"http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p1\" class=\"stimulus_reference \">\n        <div class=\"standalone_image \"></div>\n      </div>\n","stem":"<p><img src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/81b664bc/img_000_d066026b.png\" alt=\"The figure presents quadrilateral A, C D F, where side A, F and side C D are horizontal, and side C D lies above side A, F. Side C D is longer than side A, F. Point B lies on left side A, C, and point E lies on right side D F. Line segment B E, which is horizontal, divides quadrilateral A, C D F into two quadrilaterals, A, B E F and B C D E.\" width=\"107\" height=\"82\">\n          <p class=\"stem_paragraph \">In the figure above, <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/81b664bc/img_001_b4fa4e1a.png\" alt=\"side A, F \"></span></span>, <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/81b664bc/img_002_8b12b353.png\" alt=\"line segment B E \"></span></span>, and <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/81b664bc/img_003_a95e1fc3.png\" alt=\"side C D \"></span></span> are parallel. Points <span class=\"italic\">B</span> and <span class=\"italic\">E</span> lie on <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/81b664bc/img_004_80840f01.png\" alt=\"side A, C  \"></span></span> and <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/81b664bc/img_005_9f84cd43.png\" alt=\"side F D \"></span></span>, respectively. If <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/81b664bc/img_006_2e9a08ce.png\" alt=\"the length of line segment A, B equals 9, the length of line segment B C equals 18 point 5\"></span></span>, and <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/81b664bc/img_007_2b750cc7.png\" alt=\"the length of line segment F E equals 8 point 5\"></span></span>, what is the length of <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/81b664bc/img_008_d1467cb0.png\" alt=\"line segment E D \"></span></span>, to the nearest tenth?</p></p>\n","answerOptions":[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">16.8</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">17.5</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">18.4</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">19.6</p>\n"}],"keys":null,"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is correct. Since <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/81b664bc/img_009_884ebce8.png\" alt=\"line segment A F\"></span>, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/81b664bc/img_010_6710a4ef.png\" alt=\"line segment B E\"></span>, and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/81b664bc/img_011_b1e93367.png\" alt=\"line segment C D \"></span> are parallel, quadrilaterals <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/81b664bc/img_012_cd90b0f0.png\" alt=\"A F E B \"></span> and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/81b664bc/img_013_0b4a4b68.png\" alt=\"B E D C \"></span> are similar. Let <span class=\"italic\">x</span> represent the length of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/81b664bc/img_014_d1467cb0.png\" alt=\"line segment E D\"></span>. With similar figures, the ratios of the lengths of corresponding sides are equal. It follows that <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/81b664bc/img_015_a646b304.png\" alt=\"9 over 18 point 5, equals 8 point 5 over x\"></span>. Multiplying both sides of this equation by 18.5 and by <span class=\"italic\">x</span> yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/81b664bc/img_016_2f07dc94.png\" alt=\"9 x equals, 18 point 5, times 8 point 5\"></span>, or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/81b664bc/img_017_b57621f4.png\" alt=\"9 x equals 157 point 2 5\"></span>. Dividing both sides of this equation by 9 yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/81b664bc/img_018_574e4ce5.png\" alt=\"x equals 17 point 4 7\"></span>, which to the nearest tenth is 17.5.<p>Choices A, C, and D are incorrect and may result from errors made when setting up the proportion.</p></p>\n","answer_style":"Multiple Choice","section":"Math","image_count":19,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959636,"pPcc":"SAT#S","questionId":"81b664bc","skill_cd":"S.B.","score_band_range_cd":4,"skill_desc":"Lines, angles, and triangles","createDate":1691007959636,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Geometry and Trigonometry","ibn":"08390-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"S","uId":"192bcb7a-635b-41af-b757-ac401ae4eda3","difficulty":"M"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"08390-DC","section":"Math","body":"<div xmlns=\"http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p1\" class=\"stimulus_reference \">\n        <div class=\"standalone_image \"></div>\n      </div>\n","prompt":"<p><img src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"The figure presents quadrilateral A, C D F, where side A, F and side C D are horizontal, and side C D lies above side A, F. Side C D is longer than side A, F. Point B lies on left side A, C, and point E lies on right side D F. Line segment B E, which is horizontal, divides quadrilateral A, C D F into two quadrilaterals, A, B E F and B C D E.\" width=\"107\" height=\"82\">\n          <p class=\"stem_paragraph \">In the figure above, <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"side A, F \"></span></span>, <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"line segment B E \"></span></span>, and <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"side C D \"></span></span> are parallel. Points <span class=\"italic\">B</span> and <span class=\"italic\">E</span> lie on <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"side A, C  \"></span></span> and <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"side F D \"></span></span>, respectively. If <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the length of line segment A, B equals 9, the length of line segment B C equals 18 point 5\"></span></span>, and <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the length of line segment F E equals 8 point 5\"></span></span>, what is the length of <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"line segment E D \"></span></span>, to the nearest tenth?</p></p>\n","answer":{"style":"Multiple Choice","choices":{"a":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">16.8</p>\n"},"b":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">17.5</p>\n"},"c":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">18.4</p>\n"},"d":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">19.6</p>\n"}},"correct_choice":"b","rationale":"<p>Choice B is correct. Since <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"line segment A F\"></span>, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"line segment B E\"></span>, and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"line segment C D \"></span> are parallel, quadrilaterals <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"A F E B \"></span> and <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"B E D C \"></span> are similar. Let <span class=\"italic\">x</span> represent the length of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"line segment E D\"></span>. With similar figures, the ratios of the lengths of corresponding sides are equal. It follows that <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"9 over 18 point 5, equals 8 point 5 over x\"></span>. Multiplying both sides of this equation by 18.5 and by <span class=\"italic\">x</span> yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"9 x equals, 18 point 5, times 8 point 5\"></span>, or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"9 x equals 157 point 2 5\"></span>. Dividing both sides of this equation by 9 yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x equals 17 point 4 7\"></span>, which to the nearest tenth is 17.5.<p>Choices A, C, and D are incorrect and may result from errors made when setting up the proportion.</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959636,"updateDate":1691007959636}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959636, 1691007959636),
    ($SATQ$82c8325f$SATQ$, $SATQ$10d4dc39-2d6d-4fb6-8cc4-828292d3cbe0$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$f6b8637e-a490-419e-9be0-72d577a26c61$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Geometry and Trigonometry$SATQ$, $SATQ$S$SATQ$, $SATQ$S.D.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Circles$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 5, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">A circle in the&nbsp;<em>xy</em>-plane has its center at&nbsp;<math alttext="left parenthesis negative 4 comma 5 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced></math> and the point <math alttext="left parenthesis negative 8 comma 8 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced></math> lies on the circle. Which equation represents this circle?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"0ad3e044-7e4f-4274-b3f2-8c7f30ccde9e","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 4 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y plus 5 right parenthesis squared equals 5\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p>"},{"id":"80f090cc-67af-4865-abd7-a3dc4943fe4a","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis x plus 4 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus 5 right parenthesis squared equals 5\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p>"},{"id":"1e047e01-4d8c-4129-9aca-2257b7b5265d","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 4 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y plus 5 right parenthesis squared equals 25\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn></math></p>"},{"id":"82d0c179-e7c0-4a52-bf73-09dadf9c7c5b","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis x plus 4 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus 5 right parenthesis squared equals 25\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn></math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["82d0c179-e7c0-4a52-bf73-09dadf9c7c5b"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is correct. A circle in the <em>xy</em>-plane can be represented by an equation of the form&nbsp;<math alttext="left parenthesis x minus h right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus k right parenthesis squared equals r squared"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, where&nbsp;<math alttext="left parenthesis h comma k right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is the center of the circle and <math alttext="r"><mi>r</mi>
</math> is the length of a radius of the circle. It's given that the circle has its center at&nbsp;<math alttext="left parenthesis negative 4 comma 5 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Therefore, <math alttext="h equals negative 4"><mrow>
	<mi>h</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn>
</mrow>
</math> and <math alttext="k equals 5"><mrow>
	<mi>k</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>5</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Substituting <math alttext="negative 4"><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="h"><mi>h</mi>
</math> and <math alttext="5"><mn>5</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="k"><mi>k</mi>
</math> in the equation&nbsp;<math alttext="left parenthesis x minus h right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus k right parenthesis squared equals r squared"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> yields&nbsp;<math alttext="left parenthesis x minus left parenthesis negative 4 right parenthesis right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus 5 right parenthesis squared equals r squared"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, or&nbsp;<math alttext="left parenthesis x plus 4 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus 5 right parenthesis squared equals r squared"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. It's also given that the point&nbsp;<math alttext="left parenthesis negative 8 comma 8 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> lies on the circle. Substituting <math alttext="negative 8"><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> and <math alttext="8"><mn>8</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math> in the equation <math alttext="left parenthesis x plus 4 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus 5 right parenthesis squared equals r squared"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> yields&nbsp;<math alttext="left parenthesis negative 8 plus 4 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis 8 minus 5 right parenthesis squared equals r squared"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, or <math alttext="left parenthesis negative 4 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis 3 right parenthesis squared equals r squared"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, which is equivalent to&nbsp;<math alttext="16 plus 9 equals r squared"><mn>16</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, or&nbsp;<math alttext="25 equals r squared"><mn>25</mn><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. Substituting <math alttext="25"><mn>25</mn>
</math> for <math alttext="r squared"><msup>
	<mi>r</mi>
	<mn>2</mn>
</msup>
</math> in the equation&nbsp;<math alttext="left parenthesis x plus 4 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus 5 right parenthesis squared equals r squared"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> yields&nbsp;<math alttext="left parenthesis x plus 4 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus 5 right parenthesis squared equals 25"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn></math>. Thus, the equation&nbsp;<math alttext="left parenthesis x plus 4 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y minus 5 right parenthesis squared equals 25"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn></math> represents the circle.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. The circle represented by this equation has its center at&nbsp;<math alttext="left parenthesis 4 comma negative 5 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, not&nbsp;<math alttext="left parenthesis negative 4 comma 5 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, and the point&nbsp;<math alttext="left parenthesis negative 8 comma 8 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> doesn't lie on the circle.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. The point&nbsp;<math alttext="left parenthesis negative 8 comma 8 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> doesn't lie on the circle represented by this equation.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect. The circle represented by this equation has its center at <math alttext="left parenthesis 4 comma negative 5 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, not <math alttext="left parenthesis negative 4 comma 5 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, and the point&nbsp;<math alttext="left parenthesis negative 8 comma 8 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> doesn't lie on the circle.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"82c8325f","external_id":"10d4dc39-2d6d-4fb6-8cc4-828292d3cbe0","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"f6b8637e-a490-419e-9be0-72d577a26c61","uId":"f38efee1-107c-4b23-acc9-7a96ab256b59","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"S","domain":"Geometry and Trigonometry","skill_cd":"S.D.","skill_desc":"Circles","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":5,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A circle in the&nbsp;<em>xy</em>-plane has its center at&nbsp;<math alttext=\"left parenthesis negative 4 comma 5 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced></math> and the point <math alttext=\"left parenthesis negative 8 comma 8 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced></math> lies on the circle. Which equation represents this circle?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"0ad3e044-7e4f-4274-b3f2-8c7f30ccde9e","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis x minus 4 right parenthesis squared plus left parenthesis y plus 5 right parenthesis squared equals 5\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><m